# AI Trend Agent

An AI trend monitoring project that combines course curriculum knowledge with
fresh signals from official RSS feeds and GitHub releases. Curriculum content
is ingested into a local Chroma vector store so later agent workflows can
retrieve relevant, citable course material.

## Project layout

```text
01_data/curriculum/       Course slide decks, grouped by week
02_src/
   curriculum_ingest.py    Extract and index PDF/PPTX curriculum content
   monitoring_github.py    Fetch recent GitHub releases
   monitoring_rss.py       Fetch recent official blog posts
   schemas.py              Shared RawSignal and trend-analysis schemas
vectorstore/              Local generated Chroma database
```

## Setup

Use Python 3.10 or newer, then install the dependencies:

```powershell
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install chromadb python-pptx pdfplumber feedparser requests pydantic
```

The monitoring scripts can be run from `02_src`, or from the repository root
with the commands shown below. No API key is required for RSS monitoring or
local Chroma embeddings.

## Curriculum ingestion

Course slides are not stored in this repository because of their size and
redistribution restrictions. Download them from the course source and place
each PDF or PPTX in the matching `week_NN` directory, for example:

```text
01_data/curriculum/
   week_02/
      RAG_Introduction.pptx
   week_03/
      Agents_and_Tools.pdf
```

Ingest the curriculum into Chroma:

```powershell
python 02_src/curriculum_ingest.py --curriculum 01_data/curriculum --db ./vectorstore
```

Re-running ingestion is incremental: stable chunk IDs update existing content
instead of creating duplicates. To query the resulting store:

```powershell
python 02_src/curriculum_ingest.py --db ./vectorstore --query "LangChain agents"
python 02_src/curriculum_ingest.py --db ./vectorstore --query "chunking" --week 2
```

## Monitor RSS feeds

Fetch recent posts from the configured official tool blogs:

```powershell
python 02_src/monitoring_rss.py
python 02_src/monitoring_rss.py --days 60
python 02_src/monitoring_rss.py --check
```

## Monitor GitHub releases

Fetch recent releases from the watched project repositories:

```powershell
python 02_src/monitoring_github.py
python 02_src/monitoring_github.py --days 60
python 02_src/monitoring_github.py --repo langchain-ai/langchain
```

Unauthenticated GitHub requests are limited to 60 per hour. For the higher
limit, create a token with no scopes and set it locally as `GITHUB_TOKEN`:

```powershell
$env:GITHUB_TOKEN = "your-token"
```

Never commit the token. `.env` files are ignored by Git.

## Generated files

`vectorstore/`, Python caches, virtual environments, logs, secrets, and course
materials are excluded by `.gitignore`. Delete `vectorstore/` if you need to
rebuild the local index from scratch.